<h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
<section class="panel">
    <h2>About this service</h2>
    <p>Xenon is a tool for managing moderation. The person or organization running this service (the operator) is responsible for it, its moderation policy and decisions, and any extra terms for using it. The operator is not necessarily the software's author or contributors.</p>
    <p>These general terms explain how you may use Xenon. They do not say who runs this service or replace information the operator must provide by law. Before using it, read the operator's contact details, moderation policy and any extra terms.</p>
    <h2>Access and account security</h2>
    <p>To administer this service, you must sign in with a Bluesky account and be an active team member with the right permissions. Signing in alone does not give you those permissions. The operator may limit, suspend or remove your access.</p>
    <p>Use only your own account with permission to access this service. Keep your sign-in secure and sign out on shared devices. Do not share passwords, session cookies, access tokens, private keys or other sign-in details.</p>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Follow the law and stay within your team permissions. Do not bypass access checks, view information you are not allowed to see, disrupt the service, or submit material intended to cause harm or information you know is misleading.</p>
    <p>Include only information needed for moderation. Do not put passwords, access tokens, private keys or unrelated sensitive personal information in reports, notes or reasons for actions. Keep private reports and case information confidential. Share them only when you have permission and the law allows it.</p>
    <h2>Moderation actions and review</h2>
    <p>Before confirming an action, check the account or content, the label, the content version if one is specified, and your reason. Labels, decisions and team changes can have lasting effects. The service keeps a record of them.</p>
    <p>A report is not proof of wrongdoing and does not automatically apply a label. The operator's moderation policy governs decisions and appeals. An appeal does not guarantee a particular result. Use the operator's published contact details to ask for a review.</p>
    <p>If this service publishes labels, other services may keep copies and use them to display or filter content. Withdrawing a label, closing a case or deleting data here does not guarantee that copies elsewhere will be removed.</p>
    <h2>Availability and software</h2>
    <p>This service is not guaranteed to be always available, respond within a particular time, or keep working with other account and data services. Maintenance, failures or changes can interrupt access. If you cannot tell whether an action succeeded, stop and contact the operator. A failed request does not necessarily mean nothing changed.</p>
    <p>The source code uses the <a href="https://github.com/blowdart/idunno.Bluesky/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>. That license covers the software, not the operator's terms for using this service. These terms do not remove any rights or obligations that the law does not allow to be removed.</p>
    <h2>Privacy and changes</h2>
    <p>Read the <a asp-area="Xenon" asp-page="/Privacy">privacy notice</a> to learn about sign-in information, moderation records and sharing data. The operator must communicate important changes to its terms and policies, including when they take effect if the law requires it.</p>
</section>
